  "title": "emg2pose: Surface EMG and Hand Pose",
  "description": "A NEMAR re-host and EMG-BIDS conversion of the public Meta emg2pose benchmark, pairing 2 kHz, 16-channel wrist surface electromyography with hand pose labels from a 26-camera motion-capture system. The release spans 193 users, about 370 hours, 29 behavioral stages and roughly 80 million labeled frames. It supports research on estimating hand pose from surface EMG.",
  "methods_description": "Wrist sEMG was recorded at 2 kHz over 16 channels, with hand pose labels captured by a 26-camera motion-capture rig. Upstream HDF5 recordings were converted to EMG-BIDS BDF files containing 16 EMG channels and 20 joint-angle channels in radians (MISC). BAD_IK annotations mark samples where the inverse-kinematics labels are all zero.",
